  "title": "The Button Garden Expedition",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "miniature adventure",
  "premise": "A thimble-sized gardener needs to plant one bright seed in a neglected button box, but the smooth button surfaces offer nowhere to root. They discover a thread-filled buttonhole, nest the seed in it, and grow a fictional thread-flower that ties the scattered buttons into a garden path.",
  "hook": "Every island has holes. One is a home.",
  "visible_action": "Buttons tilt like islands; seed slides off polished surfaces; it settles in a threaded hole; yarn petals unfurl.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A feature that looks like a gap can become the useful place.",
  "gate": "The seed and thread-flower are magical; not a horticultural claim or child-safe craft instruction.",
